/-!
# Derived completion computed on the sections over an object

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, `𝓘 ⊂ 𝒪` a finite type sheaf of ideals and `K ↦ K^∧` the derived
completion of [Stacks, Tag 099F]. Let `U` be an object of `𝒞` over which `𝓘` is generated as an
ideal sheaf by sections `f_1, …, f_r ∈ 𝓘(U)`, and set `A = 𝒪(U)` and `I = (f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ A`.
[Stacks, Tag 0CQI] computes
```
RΓ(U, K^∧) = RΓ(U, K)^∧
```
in `D(A)`, the completion on the right being the derived completion along `I`.

`I` is the ideal of `A` generated by the chosen sections, and is *not* `𝓘(U)`: the source warns
that the two may differ, and they do, because a section of `𝓘` over `U` is only locally a
combination of the `f_i`. Everything below is stated with `I = (f_1, …, f_r)`;
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.localIdeal_le_sections` is the one inclusion that does hold.

The derived category of `𝒪`-modules meant throughout is the one of `HasDerivedCategory.standard`
on `SheafOfModules.{u} (ringSheaf X)`, installed below as a local instance; no global
`HasDerivedCategory` instance applies to a general ringed site, so that is the category these
statements denote.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionRing`: the ring `A = 𝒪(U)` of sections over an object.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleSectionsOver`: `Γ(U, -) : Mod(𝒪) ⥤ ModuleCat A` for `A` a
  ring mapping to `𝒪(U)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedSectionsOver`: `RΓ(U, -) : D(𝒪) ⥤ D(A)`, its total right
  derived functor on the unbounded derived category.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedSectionsOverObject`: the same for `A = 𝒪(U)`, which is the
  `RΓ(U, -)` of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI].
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver`: the property that `𝓘` is
  generated as an ideal sheaf by `f_1, …, f_r ∈ 𝓘(U)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.localIdeal`: the ideal `I = (f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ A`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.localIdeal_le_sections`: `I ⊆ 𝓘(U)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isNilpotent_of_mem_localIdeal`: every element of `I` is nilpotent
  when the local sections of `𝓘` are.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_map_derivedCompletionUnit_derivedSectionsOverObject` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_derivedSectionsOverObject`: [Stacks, Tag 0CQI]
  for a sheaf of ideals whose local sections are nilpotent.
* `isIso_map_derivedCompletionUnit_derivedSectionsOverObject_of_forall_isNilpotent`: the left hand
  side with the derived completion functor of [Stacks, Tag 099F] produced from that hypothesis
  rather than assumed.

## Implementation notes

*`RΓ(U, -)`.* `Γ(U, -)` is `SheafOfModules.evaluation` at `U`, whose values are modules over
`𝒪(U)`, followed by restriction of scalars along a ring map `ρ : A ⟶ 𝒪(U)`; taking `ρ` to be the
identity of `𝒪(U)` gives the `A = 𝒪(U)` of the source. `RΓ(U, -)` is its *total* right derived
functor on the unbounded `D(𝒪)`, which exists because `Mod(𝒪)` is Grothendieck abelian and so
has functorial K-injective resolutions
(`Stacks.Cohomology.Localization.hasRightDerivedFunctorOfGrothendieck`). The unbounded functor is
what Tag 0CQI needs: `K^∧` is not known to be bounded below, that resting on the Koszul formula
[Stacks, Tag 0A0E] for sheaves of modules on a site.

The ring map `ρ` is carried, as in `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleGlobalSectionsOver`; the
statements of Tag 0CQI below fix `A = 𝒪(U)` and `ρ = id`.

*The regime of the main results.* They are stated for a sheaf of ideals all of whose local
sections are nilpotent, where the derived completion functor of [Stacks, Tag 099F] is given by
`isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_isFiniteType_of_forall_isNilpotent`. There the sections
`f_i` of `𝓘` over `U` are nilpotent in `A`, hence so is every element of `I`, and both
completions are the identity: `K ⟶ K^∧` is invertible on `D(𝒪)`, and `RΓ(U, K)` is already
`I`-derived complete. The two results are the two halves of the source's equality, and neither
uses `I = 𝓘(U)`.

`isIso_map_derivedCompletionUnit_derivedSectionsOverObject` takes the `IsRightAdjoint` instance
which gives the completion functor on `D(𝒪)` as an argument, while
`isIso_map_derivedCompletionUnit_derivedSectionsOverObject_of_forall_isNilpotent` produces it
from the nilpotence hypothesis inside its statement.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0999](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0999)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQI)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

section DerivedSections

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) (U : X.C)

/-- The ring `A = 𝒪(U)` of sections of the structure sheaf over an object `U` of the site. -/
abbrev sectionRing : Type u := X.O.obj.obj (op U)

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
  (ρ : A →+* ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op U))

/-- **`Γ(U, -) : Mod(𝒪) ⥤ ModuleCat A`**, the sections of a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules over the object
`U`, regarded as an `A`-module by restriction of scalars along `ρ : A ⟶ 𝒪(U)`. -/
abbrev moduleSectionsOver :
    SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A :=
  SheafOfModules.evaluation ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (op U) ⋙
    ModuleCat.restrictScalars ρ

/-- The functor `Γ(U, -) : Mod(𝒪) ⥤ ModuleCat A` is additive. -/
instance moduleSectionsOver_additive : (moduleSectionsOver X U ρ).Additive := by
  let : (SheafOfModules.forget.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).Additive :=
    SheafOfModules.instAdditivePresheafOfModulesObjFunctorOppositeRingCatIsSheafForget _
  let : (PresheafOfModules.evaluation.{u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj (op U)).Additive :=
    PresheafOfModules.instAdditiveModuleCatCarrierObjOppositeRingCatEvaluation _ _
  let : (SheafOfModules.evaluation.{u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) (op U)).Additive :=
    CategoryTheory.Functor.instAdditiveComp
      (SheafOfModules.forget.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
      (PresheafOfModules.evaluation.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj (op U))
  let : (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} ρ).Additive := ModuleCat.instAdditiveRestrictScalars ρ
  exact CategoryTheory.Functor.instAdditiveComp
    (SheafOfModules.evaluation.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) (op U))
    (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} ρ)

/-- Sections over `U` read on the homotopy category of cochain complexes of `𝒪`-modules, with
values in `D(A)`. Its total right derived functor is `derivedSectionsOver`. -/
abbrev homotopySectionsOver :
    HomotopyCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) ⥤
      DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
  (moduleSectionsOver X U ρ).mapHomotopyCategory (ComplexShape.up ℤ) ⋙ DerivedCategory.Qh

/-- **`RΓ(U, -) : D(𝒪) ⥤ D(A)`**, derived sections over an object of the site, on the whole
unbounded derived category. It exists because `Mod(𝒪)` is Grothendieck abelian, hence has
functorial K-injective resolutions. -/
abbrev derivedSectionsOver :
    DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ⥤
      DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
  (homotopySectionsOver X U ρ).totalRightDerived DerivedCategory.Qh
    (HomotopyCategory.quasiIso (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ))

/-- The canonical comparison from termwise sections over `U` to their total right derived
functor. -/
abbrev derivedSectionsOverUnit :
    homotopySectionsOver X U ρ ⟶ DerivedCategory.Qh ⋙ derivedSectionsOver X U ρ :=
  (homotopySectionsOver X U ρ).totalRightDerivedUnit DerivedCategory.Qh
    (HomotopyCategory.quasiIso (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ))

/-- The comparison exhibits `derivedSectionsOver` as the right derived functor of sections over
`U`, which is the universal property characterizing it. -/
instance derivedSectionsOver_isRightDerivedFunctor :
    (derivedSectionsOver X U ρ).IsRightDerivedFunctor (derivedSectionsOverUnit X U ρ)
      (HomotopyCategory.quasiIso
        (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) (ComplexShape.up ℤ)) :=
  inferInstance

/-- **`RΓ(U, -) : D(𝒪) ⥤ D(𝒪(U))`**, derived sections over `U` as a complex of modules over
`A = 𝒪(U)` itself. This is the `RΓ(U, -)` of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI]. -/
abbrev derivedSectionsOverObject :
    DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ⥤
      DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} (sectionRing X U)) :=
  derivedSectionsOver X U (RingHom.id (sectionRing X U))

end DerivedSections

section LocalIdeal

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))) (U : X.C)
  {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → sectionRing X U)

/-- **`𝓘` is generated as an ideal sheaf by `f_1, …, f_r ∈ 𝓘(U)`.** The sections `f_i` lie in
`𝓘` over `U`, and every local section of `𝓘` is, locally on the site, an `𝒪`-linear combination
of their restrictions.

The second condition is local, as generation of a sheaf of ideals must be: a section of `𝓘` over
`V` becomes a combination of the `f_i` only after restriction along the arrows of some covering
sieve of `V`. That is exactly why the ideal `localIdeal` the `f_i` generate in `𝒪(U)` need not be
all of `𝓘(U)`. -/
def IsGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver : Prop :=
  (∀ i, f i ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op U)) ∧
    ∀ (V : X.C) (s : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op V)),
      s ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op V) →
      ∃ S : Sieve V, S ∈ X.J V ∧
        ∀ ⦃W : X.C⦄ (g : W ⟶ V), S g →
          ∃ (h : W ⟶ U) (c : Fin r → ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op W)),
            ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.map g.op s =
              ∑ i, c i * ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.map h.op (f i)

/-- **The ideal `I = (f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ A`** of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI], generated in `A = 𝒪(U)` by the
chosen sections. It is the ideal the right hand side of that tag completes along, and it is not
`𝓘(U)`; see `localIdeal_le_sections`. -/
def localIdeal : Ideal (sectionRing X U) := Ideal.span (Set.range f)

/-- The generators lie in the ideal they generate. -/
theorem self_mem_localIdeal (i : Fin r) : f i ∈ localIdeal X U f :=
  Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩

/-- **`I ⊆ 𝓘(U)`**: the ideal generated by `f_1, …, f_r` in `𝒪(U)` consists of sections of `𝓘`
over `U`, the `f_i` being such sections and `𝓘(U)` being a submodule.

This is the one inclusion available. The reverse fails in general — the warning of
[Stacks, Tag 0CQI] — because membership in `𝓘` is local: a section of `𝓘` over `U` is a
combination of the `f_i` only after restriction along a covering sieve, and those local
coefficients need not glue. -/
theorem localIdeal_le_sections (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op U))
    (x : sectionRing X U) (hx : x ∈ localIdeal X U f) :
    x ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op U) :=
  Submodule.span_le.2 (Set.range_subset_iff.2 hf) hx

/-- **Every element of `I` is nilpotent** when every local section of `𝓘` is and the generators
`f_i` are sections of `𝓘` over `U`. -/
theorem isNilpotent_of_mem_localIdeal
    (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op U))
    (hnil : ∀ (V : X.C) (g : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op V)),
      g ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op V) → IsNilpotent g)
    (x : sectionRing X U) (hx : x ∈ localIdeal X U f) : IsNilpotent x :=
  (Ideal.span_le (I := nilradical _)).2
    (Set.range_subset_iff.2 fun i => hnil U (f i) (hf i)) hx

end LocalIdeal

section Nilpotent

/-- Countable products exist in the derived category of a module category. -/
local instance hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory_sectionRing
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] :
    HasProductsOfShape ℕ (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) :=
  Stacks.DerivedProducts.hasProductsOfShape_derivedCategory

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))) (U : X.C)
  {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → sectionRing X U)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0CQI], the left hand side, for a sheaf of ideals with nilpotent sections.**
The canonical map `RΓ(U, K) ⟶ RΓ(U, K^∧)` is invertible.

Together with `isDerivedComplete_derivedSectionsOverObject`, whose content is that the right hand
side `RΓ(U, K)^∧` is `RΓ(U, K)` as well, this is the equality `RΓ(U, K^∧) = RΓ(U, K)^∧` of the
source in this regime, compatibly with the canonical maps on both sides. -/
@[stacks 0CQI "the left hand side: the canonical map `RΓ(U, K) ⟶ RΓ(U, K^∧)` is invertible, for a
  sheaf of ideals of finite type all of whose local sections are nilpotent — the hypothesis under
  which this library has the derived completion functor of [Stacks, Tag 099F]. The equality with
  `RΓ(U, K)^∧` is this together with `isDerivedComplete_derivedSectionsOverObject`. The general
  case needs [Stacks, Tags 0A0F, 0BLX]; the first is `derivedCompletion_restrict`, the second is
  not available as an identity here"]
theorem isIso_map_derivedCompletionUnit_derivedSectionsOverObject
    [𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]
    [(ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X 𝓘)).IsRightAdjoint]
    (hgen : IsGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver X 𝓘 U f)
    (hnil : ∀ (V : X.C) (g : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op V)),
      g ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op V) → IsNilpotent g)
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))) :
    IsIso ((derivedSectionsOverObject X U).map ((derivedCompletionUnit X 𝓘).app K)) := by
  obtain ⟨-, -⟩ := hgen
  have hiso : IsIso ((derivedCompletionUnit X 𝓘).app K) :=
    isIso_derivedCompletionUnit_app X 𝓘
      (isDerivedComplete_of_forall_isNilpotent X 𝓘 hnil K)
  exact (derivedSectionsOverObject X U).map_isIso _

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0CQI], the left hand side, for a sheaf of ideals with nilpotent sections, with
the derived completion functor produced rather than assumed.** This is
`isIso_map_derivedCompletionUnit_derivedSectionsOverObject` without its `IsRightAdjoint` instance
argument: the left adjoint of the inclusion of derived complete objects is discharged inside the
statement from the nilpotence hypothesis, by
`isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_isFiniteType_of_forall_isNilpotent`. -/
@[stacks 0CQI "the left hand side: the canonical map `RΓ(U, K) ⟶ RΓ(U, K^∧)` is invertible, for a
  sheaf of ideals of finite type all of whose local sections are nilpotent — the hypothesis under
  which this library has the derived completion functor of [Stacks, Tag 099F]. That functor is
  *produced* from the nilpotence hypothesis rather than assumed: the `IsRightAdjoint` instance is
  discharged inside the statement. The equality with `RΓ(U, K)^∧` is this together with
  `isDerivedComplete_derivedSectionsOverObject`. The general case needs
  [Stacks, Tags 0A0F, 0BLX]; the first is `derivedCompletion_restrict`, the second is not
  available as an identity here"]
theorem isIso_map_derivedCompletionUnit_derivedSectionsOverObject_of_forall_isNilpotent
    [𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]
    (hgen : IsGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver X 𝓘 U f)
    (hnil : ∀ (V : X.C) (g : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op V)),
      g ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op V) → IsNilpotent g)
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))) :
    letI : (ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X 𝓘)).IsRightAdjoint :=
      isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_isFiniteType_of_forall_isNilpotent X 𝓘 hnil
    IsIso ((derivedSectionsOverObject X U).map ((derivedCompletionUnit X 𝓘).app K)) := by
  let : (ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X 𝓘)).IsRightAdjoint :=
    isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_isFiniteType_of_forall_isNilpotent X 𝓘 hnil
  exact isIso_map_derivedCompletionUnit_derivedSectionsOverObject X 𝓘 U f hgen hnil K

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0CQI], the right hand side, for a sheaf of ideals with nilpotent sections.**
`RΓ(U, K)` is derived complete along `I = (f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ A = 𝒪(U)`, so its derived completion is
itself.

Together with `isIso_map_derivedCompletionUnit_derivedSectionsOverObject` this is the equality
`RΓ(U, K^∧) = RΓ(U, K)^∧` of the source in this regime. The completion is along the ideal
generated by the chosen sections, not along `𝓘(U)`. -/
@[stacks 0CQI "the right hand side `RΓ(U, K)^∧`, identified with `RΓ(U, K)` by its being already
  derived complete along `I = (f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ 𝒪(U)`, for a sheaf of ideals all of whose local
  sections are nilpotent. The completion is along the ideal the chosen sections generate and not
  along `𝓘(U)`, which the source warns need not be the same ideal"]
theorem isDerivedComplete_derivedSectionsOverObject
    (hgen : IsGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver X 𝓘 U f)
    (hnil : ∀ (V : X.C) (g : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op V)),
      g ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj (op V) → IsNilpotent g)
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))) :
    _root_.IsDerivedComplete (localIdeal X U f)
      ((derivedSectionsOverObject X U).obj K) := by
  intro a ha
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := isNilpotent_of_mem_localIdeal X 𝓘 U f hgen.1 hnil a ha
  refine isDerivedCompleteAt_of_isNilpotent ⟨n, ?_⟩
  rw [smul_pow, hn, zero_smul]

end Nilpotent

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
